fact WorkItem(id: "WI-726", description: some(value: "Typer: an operation's explicit type param bound to its parent sort's own type param (Relation[T = L] on a member of sort Relation) is aliased onto the sort's CANONICAL shared T var at load, so the explicit param never binds independently. Two such params (join[L,R](r1: Relation[T=L], r2: Relation[T=R])) collapse onto one canonical Relation.T: r1 binds it to schema-1, r2 to schema-2 -> contradiction (enforce_member_tie) / the type params surface as UnconstrainedTypeParam. This is the parametricity-tie (WI-374) firing where it should NOT: a member op that DECLARES distinct explicit type params for its self-sort refs intends them INDEPENDENT (unlike union(a: Relation, b: Relation) which shares bare Relation and WANTS the tie). DIAGNOSIS (WI-714 join): unify_parameterized_view unifies the T slot fine, but the param's T var was already aliased to canonical Relation.T at load, so bind_resolved targets canonical-T (name 'T'), never the declared L/R; check_unconstrained_type_params then flags L. FIX DIRECTION: when a member op's self-sort-ref param carries an EXPLICIT type-param binding (Relation[T = L]), keep L distinct from the sort's canonical T (honor the explicit param) instead of collapsing it onto the canonical channel; then enforce_member_tie must not tie the two independent params. Blocks WI-714 join as a Relation MEMBER with the dot form (person_row.join(member_row, lambda (c,q) -> eq(c.name, q.who))); a namespace-level (non-member, prefix) join sidesteps it via foreign-sort expansion. Repro: the [L,R] signature in stdlib relation.anthill + wi714_join_test.rs."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-16T12:03:37Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-726", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED + committed (6185dbc2, with WI-714 join). ROOT CAUSE differed from this ticket's original text (a WRONG early hypothesis): the real cause, bisected with per-symbol instrumentation, is unify_parameterized_view matching binding params by raw SYMBOL IDENTITY (p==param), missing the canonical-key vs bare-key split -- a Relation[T=schema] VALUE keys T as anthill.prelude.Relation.T while a Relation[T=L] SIGNATURE keys it bare T -- so the T slot was silently skipped and op type param L stayed UnconstrainedTypeParam. FIX (USER chose the surgical gate over canonicalizing the 4 bare-key loader sites): same-base-gated same_label -- same_sort_canonical(a_base,b_base) ? same_label : identity. A code-review agent EMPIRICALLY CONFIRMED an UNGATED same_label PANICS on cross-base unify (List provides Stream passes the base check, then same_label(Stream.T, List.T) trips its debug_assert; release = silent mis-unify). Reachable here (Relation provides LogicalStream). Mirrors parameterized_compatible_view. Full workspace green 2891.", at: "2026-07-16T12:03:39Z")
